00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:54.360
<v Guest>So if someone is asking, I need to reset my password, I have a problem logging in,

288
00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:59.260
<v Guest>then you can really route them to the places they can get the support.

289
00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:01.640
<v Guest>So that's a very simple problem.

290
00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:07.480
<v Guest>The answer is very clear and a human can really identify this problem clearly and easily.

291
00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:13.160
<v Guest>So that's some characteristics of a Goldilocks problem for AI.

292
00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:17.260
<v Guest>Simple and a human can really easily do that.

293
00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:22.300
<v Guest>So machine can do that in a much more scalable way there.

294
00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:28.480
<v Guest>And also the other part to consider is really the problem is simple, but the impact of solving

295
00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.280
<v Guest>big. The password reset or

296
00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:33.280
<v Guest>user login in those customer

297
00:21:33.280 --> 00:21:35.020
<v Guest>requests for Autodesk happens

298
00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:36.800
<v Guest>thousands of times every month.

299
00:21:37.240 --> 00:21:39.100
<v Guest>So the impact actually is much

300
00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:41.220
<v Guest>big, right? The last but not

301
00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:43.220
<v Guest>least, there's also need

302
00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:44.720
<v Guest>to be good quality data exist.

303
00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:47.320
<v Guest>We know that AI need high quality

304
00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.340
<v Guest>training data. Your AI

305
00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:51.340
<v Guest>initiative won't be successful if you don't

306
00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:53.140
<v Guest>have access to high quality training data.

