00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:53.840
<v Guest>And when he got to Tesla, it was the opposite, right?

329
00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:55.700
<v Guest>It was 80% of time spent on training data

330
00:22:55.700 --> 00:22:57.900
<v Guest>and like 20% spent on model building.

331
00:22:59.260 --> 00:23:06.000
<v Guest>it up. And the challenge that Tesla and many others have is that how do you get enough

332
00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:13.840
<v Guest>examples of real world problems to be able to train a self-driving car? So in this instance,

333
00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:22.040
<v Guest>it was a sad situation. What happened was Tesla was on autopilot and ended up hitting a semi truck

334
00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:27.640
<v Guest>that was perpendicular on a freeway. Now, that doesn't happen very often, right? It's very

